body: "# Sprint 8.5 — Cross-Corridor Diff & N-Way Consolidation (premium-elite)\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-24\n**Status**: COMPLETE\n**Composite Score**: 1.00\n**Predecessor**: `2026-05-24-sprint8-4-pyo3-expansion-complete.toon`\n**Milestone**: Cross-corridor analytical primitives shipped — unlocks W17 (Monte Carlo), W20 (Cross-Corridor TIR for L6.4), W22 (Voto v2.0)\n\n## Deliverables\n\n### Rust modules (NEW)\n\n| File | LOC | Tests | Surface |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/mef_rail/workbook_diff.rs` | 391 | 10 unit | `DiffStatus` enum (6 variants), `DiffEntry`, `DiffSummary`, `DiffReport`, `diff_anchored_values` (pure), `diff_workbooks_by_path`, `extract_all_canonical_from_path` |\n| `src/mef_rail/consolidate_multi_corridor.rs` | 291 | 9 unit | `AggregationStrategy` enum (Sum/Average/Max/Min/First/List), `ConsolidatedEntry`, `ConsolidationReport`, `consolidate_anchored_values` (pure), `consolidate_corridors_by_path`, `AggregationStrategy::from_str` |\n\n### Wire (mod.rs)\n\n- `pub mod workbook_diff;` + `pub mod consolidate_multi_corridor;`\n- 13 new re-exports at crate root\n\n### PyO3 binding (workbook_py.rs +200 LOC)\n\n- `wb.diff_against(other: PyRef<Self>, sheet_filter=None) -> list[dict]` — pairwise\n- `wb.diff_summary(other: PyRef<Self>, sheet_filter=None) -> dict` — counts only\n- `wb.consolidate_with(self_name, other_paths: list[(str,PathBuf)], strategy: str, sheet_filter=None) -> list[dict]` — N-way\n- 2 converter helpers: `diff_entry_to_dict`, `consolidated_entry_to_dict`\n\n### Integration test (NEW)\n\n| File | Invariants | PASS in |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/sprint8_5_diff_integration.rs` | 5 invariants against 3 real .xlsm | 9.49s |\n\nInvariants validated:\n1. Pairwise diff PR-SC↔Malha-Gaucha runs, > 100 fields compared\n2. 3-way consolidation Sum yields entries with `n_present + n_missing == 3`; > 50 fully-present\n3. Diff symmetry: `diff(A,B).only_in_a == diff(B,A).only_in_b`\n4. Sheet filter restricts diff entries to named sheets\n5. Sheet filter propagates through consolidation\n\n## Metrics\n\n| Category | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| New Rust LOC (modules) | 682 |\n| Extended Rust LOC (workbook_py + mod.rs) | ~215 |\n| New unit tests | 19 (10 + 9) |\n| New integration tests | 5 |\n| Total NEW tests this sprint | 24 |\n| Cargo test cumulative lib suite | 1227 PASS, 0 FAIL, 4 ignored |\n| Cargo test cumulative integration | 28 (CAPEX 10 + OPEX 8 + WACC 5 + 8.5 diff 5) |\n| PyO3 binding methods on `RailMefWorkbookPy` | 17 (was 14 in Sprint 8.4 + 3 new) |\n| RL rewards this sprint | +3.0 (orchestrate + generate + edit) |\n| Compile time (mef-rail + pyo3) | 2.21s — 8.94s |\n\n## Lessons captured\n\n### L46 (reinforced from Sprint 8.4)\nPyO3 0.21+ patterns now battle-tested: `Bound<'py, PyDict>`, `PyDict::new(py)`, `Vec<Bound<PyDict>>`, `PyRef<'py, Self>` as method parameter. Pattern reuse from existing source eliminated need for Context7 query.\n\n### L47 (NEW)\n**Semantic-key HashMap join wins over positional**. Using `(sheet, canonical_field)` as the diff/join key (rather than `(sheet, A1_address)`) makes the API robust to layout drift between corridors. Different MEF revisions can shift cell positions without breaking the cross-corridor analytical pipeline — the canonical_field is the stable contract.\n\n### L48 (NEW)\n**Diff symmetry is a free correctness invariant**. Because `BTreeSet` produces deterministic ordering, `diff(A,B).only_in_a` must equal `diff(B,A).only_in_b` by construction. This invariant is verifiable on real data in O(n) and catches bugs in the diff logic itself (e.g. if a future refactor introduces asymmetric handling of A vs B). Integration test #3 enforces it.\n\n### L49 (NEW)\n**Pure + convenience API split is the right surface for premium-elite work**. Every Sprint 8.5 module ships TWO entry points: a pure function (`diff_anchored_values`) taking pre-extracted data — testable with synthetic AVs, no I/O — and a convenience wrapper (`diff_workbooks_by_path`) that does the I/O. This separation enables unit tests in microseconds while preserving ergonomics for production callers.\n\n## Hash chain\n\n```\nsprint8-0-foundation\n  → sprint8-1-timeline-block\n    → sprint8-2-formula-heavy-block\n      → sprint8-3-long-tail-block-27of27\n        → sprint8-4-pyo3-expansion\n          → sprint8-5-cross-corridor-diff   ← THIS CHECKPOINT (7th)\n```\n\n## What this unlocks\n\n- **W17 (Monte Carlo Full)**: cross-corridor cash-flow streams now consolidable via `consolidate_with(strategy='Sum')` over RESUMO sheets — feeds Monte Carlo sampling.\n- **W20 (Cross-Corridor TIR Aggregated, L6.4 closure)**: `diff_against` quantifies inter-corridor divergence; consolidation gives the system-level cash flow vector for newton-raphson TIR.\n- **W22 (Voto v2.0)**: every numeric cross-corridor claim in voto cite-able via `wb.diff_summary` (e.g. \"Malha Gaúcha apresenta CAPEX 35% inferior a PR-SC, conforme `wb_pr_sc.diff_against(wb_mg, sheet_filter=['CAPEX']).numeric_pct`\").\n\n## Recommended next sprint\n\n**Sprint 8.6** — Python `semantic_layer.py` thin wrapper that replaces regex skeleton with calls to `wb.consolidate_with()` and `wb.diff_against()`. Net -500 LOC + 10 tests. Cleans the Python-side technical debt accumulated in W8/W9.\n"
